<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Cross section of a river by the trapezoidal rule</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>To find how much water the [[if test="is(ix=1)"]]Nzoia River at Bungoma[[elif test="is(ix=2)"]]Tana River at Garissa[[elif test="is(ix=3)"]]Yala River near Siaya[[elif test="is(ix=4)"]]Athi River near Kibwezi[[elif test="is(ix=5)"]]Thika River at Thika[[elif test="is(ix=6)"]]Ewaso Ng'iro River at Archers Post[[elif test="is(ix=7)"]]Sondu River near Nyakach[[elif test="is(ix=8)"]]Nyando River near Ahero[[elif test="is(ix=9)"]]Turkwel River at Lodwar[[else]]Mara River near the Mara bridge[[/if]] carries, a team stretched a rope \({@W@}\,\text{m}\) across the river and measured the depth every \({@hh@}\,\text{m}\), from one bank to the other.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Distance from bank (m)</th>[[foreach u="xs"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@u@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Depth (m)</th>[[foreach u="dall"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@exd(u)@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr></table><p>(a) Use the trapezoidal rule to estimate the area of the cross-section of the river.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The water flows at \({@exd(v)@}\,\text{m/s}\). Estimate the volume of water that passes the rope each second.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] \(\text{m}^3\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) The river bed curves like a bowl between the measured points, as in the sketch. Which statement is true?</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Sketch: a curved river bed with straight dashed lines joining the measured depths; the dashed lines lie above the bed.">[[jsxgraph width="420px" height="220px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [-0.6, 0.6, 6.6, -3.0], axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  var d = function(x) { return -2.4 * Math.sin(Math.PI * x / 6); };
  b.create('segment', [[-0.5, 0], [6.5, 0]], {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('text', [-0.5, 0.35, 'water surface (not to scale)'], {fontSize: 12, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('functiongraph', [d, 0, 6], {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 3, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  for (var k = 0; k < 4; k++) { b.create('segment', [[1.5 * k, d(1.5 * k)], [1.5 * (k + 1), d(1.5 * (k + 1))]], {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 2, dash: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false}); }
  for (var j = 1; j < 4; j++) { b.create('segment', [[1.5 * j, 0], [1.5 * j, d(1.5 * j)]], {strokeColor: '#666666', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false}); }
  b.create('text', [2.2, -2.75, 'river bed (solid curve)'], {fontSize: 12, fixed: true, highlight: false});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]</div><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) There are \({@n+1@}\) measuring points, so \({@n@}\) strips of width \(h = {@W@} \div {@n@} = {@hh@}\,\text{m}\). The depths at the banks are \(0\), but they are still ordinates. Each inner depth is a side of two trapezia, so it is counted twice:</p><p>\[A \approx \tfrac{1}{2} \times {@hh@} \times \left[0 + 0 + 2 \times {@exd(apply("+",ds))@}\right] = {@exd(A)@}\,\text{m}^2\]</p><p>(b) Each second a slice of water \({@exd(v)@}\,\text{m}\) long passes the rope, so the volume is area \(\times\) speed \(= {@exd(A)@} \times {@exd(v)@} = {@exd(Qf)@}\,\text{m}^3\) each second.</p><p>(c) The straight lines between the measured depths lie above the curved bed, so each trapezium stops short of the bed and some water is left out: the estimate is too small.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
